#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versions des packages\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le code de cette page a été développé avec les prérequis suivants.\n"
"Nous recommandons d'utiliser ces versions ou des versions plus récentes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"You can use options to customize the Executor primitive. Unlike Sampler and Estimator, Executor has very few options since the majority of the design intents is encoded in the samplex.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Notes\">\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can see the available options and update option values during or after primitive initialization.\n"
msgstr "Tu peux voir les options disponibles et mettre à jour les valeurs des options pendant ou après l'initialisation de la primitive.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `update()` method to apply changes to the `options` attribute.\n"
msgstr "Utilise la méthode `update()` pour appliquer des modifications à l'attribut `options`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `options` attribute is the `dataclass` Python type.  You can use the built-in `asdict` method to convert it to a dictionary.\n"
msgstr "L'attribut `options` est le type Python `dataclass`. Tu peux utiliser la méthode intégrée `asdict` pour le convertir en dictionnaire.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Executor can only process information encoded in samplexes. Refer to the [Samplomatic guides](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/index) to understand restrictions.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"- L'Executor ne peut traiter que les informations encodées dans des samplexes. Consulte les [guides Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/index) pour comprendre les restrictions.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pass-options\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pass-options\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set Executor options {#set-executor-options}"
msgstr "Définir les options Executor {#set-executor-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an option is specified both during and after primitive initialization, the value set after initializing the primitive is used.\n"
msgstr "Si une option est spécifiée à la fois pendant et après l'initialisation de la primitive, la valeur définie après l'initialisation de la primitive est utilisée.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Primitive initialization {#primitive-initialization}"
msgstr "Initialisation de la primitive {#primitive-initialization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can pass in an instance of the options class or a dictionary when initializing Executor, which then makes a copy of those options. Thus, changing the original dictionary or options instance doesn't affect the options owned by the primitive.\n"
msgstr "Tu peux passer une instance de la classe d'options ou un dictionnaire lors de l'initialisation d'Executor, qui fait ensuite une copie de ces options. Ainsi, la modification du dictionnaire original ou de l'instance d'options n'affecte pas les options appartenant à la primitive.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options class {#options-class}"
msgstr "Classe d'options {#options-class}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When creating an instance of the `Executor` class, you can pass in an instance of the options class. Those options are then applied when you use `run()` to perform the calculation.  Specify the options in this format:  `options.option.sub-option.sub-sub-option = choice`.  For example: `options.environment.log_level = INFO`.\n"
msgstr "Lors de la création d'une instance de la classe `Executor`, tu peux passer une instance de la classe d'options. Ces options sont ensuite appliquées lorsque tu utilises `run()` pour effectuer le calcul. Spécifie les options dans ce format : `options.option.sub-option.sub-sub-option = choice`. Par exemple : `options.environment.log_level = INFO`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Exemple :\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dictionary {#dictionary}"
msgstr "Dictionnaire {#dictionary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can specify options as a dictionary when initializing Executor.\n"
msgstr "Tu peux spécifier les options sous forme de dictionnaire lors de l'initialisation d'Executor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"options-table\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"options-table\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
